## ⚡ **ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS**

### **CI/CD Integration**
- All CI/CD pipelines MUST include comprehensive test execution AND emotional validation
- Deployments MUST be blocked if any tests fail OR trust scores drop below 4.2
- Pull requests MUST include test updates for new functionality AND emotional impact assessment
- Merge requests MUST demonstrate test coverage for changes AND emotional sovereignty preservation

### **Code Review Requirements**
- All code reviews MUST verify test coverage AND emotional resonance
- Reviewers MUST confirm tests actually validate the functionality AND user empowerment
- No code can be merged without corresponding test updates AND emotional validation
- Test quality is as important as code quality AND emotional intelligence

### **Documentation Standards**
- All feature documentation MUST include test evidence AND emotional impact assessment
- API documentation MUST include integration test examples AND trust transparency validation
- User guides MUST be validated through user acceptance tests AND empowerment confirmation
- Technical specifications MUST include test validation criteria AND emotional sovereignty requirements

### **Stakeholder Communication**
- All status reports MUST include test validation evidence AND trust metrics
- Feature demos MUST be backed by passing test suites AND emotional resonance validation
- Milestone completion MUST be proven through comprehensive testing AND user empowerment metrics
- Project success MUST be measured through test metrics AND emotional sovereignty indicators

